{{also|bohemian}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|Bohemia|ian}}

In sense of [[Romani]] and by association, marginalized artists, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|bohémien||person from [[Bohemia]], [[Romani]]}}, from {{m|fr|Bohême||[[Bohemia]]}}. Regarding the sense evolution, compare {{m|en|gypsy}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A native or resident of [[Bohemia]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[dialect]] of the [[Czech]] [[language]] spoken in Bohemia.
# {{lb|en|countable|archaic}} A [[Gypsy]], a [[Romani]].
# {{alt case|en|bohemian}}; an unconventional artist.

